DEBUGGING LOG

Question 2 – Hash Table Implementation

PRN: 202501100027

Scenario: Mango Varieties

Hash Function: Mid-Square

Collision Strategy: Separate Chaining

Commit 1 – Project Initialization

I created the project folder and initialized the Git repository. I added the personalized dataset of 20 values generated using the seed 27. I checked the generated values against the given formula to ensure that the dataset was correct.

Commit 2 – Mid-Square Hash Function

I implemented the mid-square hash function. Initially, I needed to ensure that the middle two digits were extracted consistently, especially for smaller values such as 5 and 9. I used four-digit zero-padding as the calculation convention and verified the resulting hash indices manually.

Commit 3 – Linked List Implementation

I created a Node structure containing a key and a pointer to the next node. I also initialized the hash table with 17 empty positions. I tested the linked-list structure to ensure that nodes could be connected correctly.

Commit 4 – Initial Insertion Implementation

I implemented the insertion function for storing keys at their calculated hash indices. During testing, I considered directly assigning a new node to an occupied index. This approach would overwrite the existing node and lose previously inserted data. I abandoned it and proceeded to implement proper collision handling.

Commit 5 – Separate Chaining Implementation

I implemented separate chaining using linked lists. When two or more keys generated the same hash index, the program traversed the existing chain and inserted the new node at the end. I verified the collision chains using the personalized dataset.

Commit 6 – Display Function

I implemented the display function to show all 17 hash table positions. I checked that empty positions displayed NULL and occupied positions displayed their linked-list elements in insertion order.

Commit 7 – Memory Management and Final Testing

I implemented memory cleanup using delete to release dynamically allocated nodes. I compiled and executed the final program and compared its output with my manually calculated hash table. The final result was checked for correct hash indices and collision handling.

